      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5cfb491476b5b77800e860ec|full_name}No, there are clearly quite a few creators who want to do this. In particular, there are quite a few avatars where NSFW content is prohibited (including those released by companies).\n\nThe problem is that such content can be created using those avatars.\n\nI have worked with over 20 avatar creators so far, and as a general trend, I have heard directly from them that they find it problematic when such behavior occurs in public spaces. My opinion on this matter is based on those experiences.",
